From 72d696fd5a34e3eeecde7c3aecca0168c3d1afb2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dimitri Geelen <dimitri@geelenandcompany.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:25:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] bvp estimator: automatic inception inputs with sticky
 human values, a hypothesis draft that never fabricates its success clause,
 and scores that cite the claim they argue about (from 832 T-865/T-867/T-868,
 arc-004)

Three slices of one arc, in the estimator only:
- T-865: an inception's VoI and target blast radius are ESTIMATED when absent
  (propose_inception_inputs), and a value a human wrote is STICKY: the estimator never
  overwrites it, and it reports what the guard protected (telemetry row to
  .context/telemetry/bvp-sticky.jsonl). Before, an absent or malformed VoI silently became a
  neutral 2.
- T-867: propose_hypothesis drafts the three-part ## Hypothesis from the task's own text, and
  leaves the success clause as an explicit gap when the text names nothing observable, never
  inventing a measure. Research-kind inceptions are skipped.
- T-868: every declarative score names what it is an argument ABOUT. A human-sourced hypothesis
  is cited; a machine draft is not (the machine would be citing itself); no hypothesis says so.
  Citation adds provenance only: it moves no score.
Probes (tests/unit/): test_t1021_sticky_scoring.sh 7/7, test_t1021_hypothesis_draft.sh 10/10,
test_t1021_cited_support.sh 6/6 (brings its own declarative driver, so the result does not
depend on the host's policy). On this tree before the patch, each probe refuses (TEETH BROKEN):
the functions it tests do not exist.
Unchanged before and after: tests/unit/test_bvp*.py and *bvp*.bats (24 files). One test,
bvp_auto_promote.bats #1 (OFF default), fails on both sides.
